NAME
     losetup - make a file look like a block device

SYNOPSIS
     losetup [-f] [-r] [-o OFFSET] [--sizelimit N] [--show] DEVICE FILE
     losetup -d DEVICE
     losetup -b BASE DEVICE DELTA
     losetup [-a]

DESCRIPTION
     losetup attaches FILE to a loop device, so that a file holding a
     file system can be mounted. With -b it attaches DELTA as a
     copy-on-write layer over BASE, which is what gives a cloned machine
     a disk of its own without copying the original.

OPTIONS
     -f             find a free device and use it
     -r             read-only
     -o OFFSET      start OFFSET bytes into the file
     --sizelimit N  use only N bytes of it
     --show         print the device chosen
     -d DEVICE      detach
     -a             list what is attached
     -b BASE        this device is a delta over BASE

SEE ALSO
     mount(1), mkimage(1), vmm(1)
